# Scratch directories the suite creates and (usually) removes. Derived and enforced by
# `test_scratch_ignored.py` -- a name here that the gate cannot reach is dead weight, and a scratch
# dir NOT here makes `git status` read as uncommitted work the moment a run is concurrent or crashes.
# A stop hook read `_shelf_famgeom/` exactly that way, which is what prompted this block.
_ifc_*/
_shelf_*/
_demo_capture_ifc/
_stb/
_stcobie/
test_digest_tmp/
# Gate fixture stores: `_body_param_reach_store`, `_route_reach_store`, `_route_shadow_store`.
# WIDENED from `_*_reach_store/` when ROUTE-SHADOW's gate added the third one and did not match --
# `_route_shadow_store` is not a reachability gate and renaming it to fit the glob would have been a
# lie told to a pattern. `test_scratch_ignored.py` caught it, which is what it is for. No tracked path
# matches `_*_store` (checked with `git ls-files`), so the wider glob costs nothing.
_*_store/
